# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# libre-media — host-specific configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env   then fill in the blanks below.
#
# This file is the ONLY place secrets may live (CLAUDE.md §5). It is
# git-ignored. `make migrate-check` verifies every variable here is also
# present in .env, so keep this file complete when you add a variable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public hostname. caddy-docker-proxy issues the TLS certificate for this name,
# so DNS must already resolve it to this server or ACME will fail.
SITE_HOST=photos.libreminds.org

# The EXTERNAL docker network that caddy-docker-proxy watches. We attach to it
# and never modify it (CLAUDE.md §4). Confirm with:
#   docker inspect caddy-proxy --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | grep INGRESS
CADDY_NETWORK=caddy


# --- Backblaze B2 ----------------------------------------------------------

# The bucket's FRIENDLY DOWNLOAD HOST -- hostname only, no scheme, no path.
# Format: f00X.backblazeb2.com  (the digits are your bucket's region cluster)
#
# Where to find it: B2 console -> Buckets -> your bucket -> Bucket Details.
# The "Endpoint" / "Friendly URL" shown there looks like
#     https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/libreminds-media/<key>
# and the part you want is the "f005.backblazeb2.com".
#
#   *** THIS IS NOT THE S3-COMPATIBLE ENDPOINT. ***
#
# The same Bucket Details page also shows an S3 endpoint of the form
# s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com. It is easy to copy the wrong one -- they
# differ by one line on the same screen. Do not use it here. The S3 endpoint
# serves a different URL shape (/<bucket>/<key>), so the /file/<bucket>/<key>
# path this project builds does not exist on it.
#
# SYMPTOM IF YOU GET IT WRONG: every media URL fails, and the cache proxies
# through to a Backblaze error rather than an image:
#
#     HTTP 400
#     <Error><Code>InvalidRequest</Code>
#            <Message>Unable to obtain account ...</Message></Error>
#
# The site's pages and album JSON still load fine, which makes this look like a
# broken bucket rather than a wrong hostname. Check before you start anything:
#
#     curl -sI https://$B2_DOWNLOAD_HOST/file/$B2_BUCKET/nonexistent | head -1
#         HTTP/1.1 404    <- correct host  (B2 returns a not_found JSON body)
#         HTTP/1.1 400    <- wrong host, you have the S3 endpoint
#
B2_DOWNLOAD_HOST=f005.backblazeb2.com

# Bucket name. Must be a PUBLIC bucket — the cache proxy fetches over plain
# HTTPS with no credentials. See README "Why the bucket is public".
B2_BUCKET=libreminds-media

# Application key scoped to the bucket above. Needs listFiles + readFiles +
# writeFiles. Used ONLY by the `tools` container, passed as environment
# variables so rclone never writes a config file to disk.
# Create at: B2 console -> Application Keys -> Add a New Application Key
B2_KEY_ID=
B2_APP_KEY=


# --- Media cache (nginx proxy_cache) ---------------------------------------

# Upper bound on the on-disk cache. Everything here is disposable: deleting
# cache-data/ only costs a re-fetch from B2.
#
# Sizing note for the current server: / is 203G. After reclaiming 53GB of
# Docker build cache it sits at 50% used with 98G free, which is why 20g is
# safe here. Check `make cache-stats` before raising it, and remember
# CACHE_MIN_FREE below is the real safety net.
CACHE_MAX_SIZE=20g

# Hard floor on FILESYSTEM free space. nginx evicts cache entries rather than
# let the disk drop below this, regardless of CACHE_MAX_SIZE. Requires
# nginx >= 1.19.1. This is the setting that protects the other services on
# this host from a runaway cache.
CACHE_MIN_FREE=8g

# Purge cache entries not requested within this window.
CACHE_INACTIVE=30d

# Shared-memory zone for cache keys. ~8000 keys per megabyte.
CACHE_KEYS_ZONE_SIZE=50m

# DNS resolver the cache uses to look up B2_DOWNLOAD_HOST. 127.0.0.11 is
# Docker's embedded DNS, available on any user-defined network. We resolve
# through a variable (not a literal in proxy_pass) so nginx re-resolves B2
# every 30s instead of pinning the IP it saw at boot.
# Override to 1.1.1.1 or 8.8.8.8 if a future host has no Docker DNS.
RESOLVER=127.0.0.11


# --- Cache-Control ---------------------------------------------------------

# Static pages and album JSON: short, so an edit goes live quickly.
WEB_MAX_AGE=300

# Media bytes: content-hashed filenames are immutable (CLAUDE.md §6), so a
# year is safe. A changed photo gets a new filename, never a new body.
MEDIA_MAX_AGE=31536000


# --- File ownership --------------------------------------------------------

# UID/GID the `tools` container runs as, so files it writes into web/albums/
# and inbox/ are owned by a real user instead of root.
#
# LEAVE THESE COMMENTED OUT to inherit the uid/gid of whoever runs `make`
# (the Makefile fills them in). Set them explicitly only if `make` is run by
# a different account than the one that owns the files — e.g. from cron, or
# when volunteers upload over SFTP as a shared group. See README
# "Letting volunteers upload".
#PUID=1000
#PGID=1000


# --- lightGallery ----------------------------------------------------------

# lightGallery v2 is GPLv3 and this repository is public under a compatible
# licence, so NO key is required and this stays empty.
#
# It is here only as a hook for a future commercial licence. Note that setting
# it has no effect today: web/ is served as static files with no templating,
# so the key would have to be placed in web/assets/config.js by hand. See
# MIGRATE.md "Known gaps".
LG_LICENSE_KEY=
